  "fields": {
    "title": "Pseudo Class",
    "textContent": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Description",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "A ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "3TBGoqMl1snjRBxLIzrc6Z",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "CSS",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " pseudo-class is like a visual effect you can add to specific parts of your website without changing the actual content. Imagine you can make a button change color when someone hovers over it, or style a link differently after it's been clicked. It's a way to add interactive and dynamic touches to your design elements based on certain conditions or user actions.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "A pseudo-class consists of a colon (:) followed by the pseudo-class name (e.g. :hover). The element that a pseudo-class is attached to is defined as an ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "anchor element",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " (e.g. button in case: button:hover).\n",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Possibilities",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Pseudo-classes offer various possibilities for enhancing website design and interactivity. Here are some examples:",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {
                        "target": {
                          "sys": {
                            "id": "5Kqa2ZyANgkNAtfUxAU1KP",
                            "type": "Link",
                            "linkType": "Entry"
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "data": {},
                          "marks": [],
                          "value": "Hover",
                          "nodeType": "text"
                        }
                      ],
                      "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": " Effects: Change the appearance of elements when a user moves their mouse over them. For example, making",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {
                        "target": {
                          "sys": {
                            "id": "FLAhUrwyFee8ZwKeQU40J",
                            "type": "Link",
                            "linkType": "Entry"
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "data": {},
                          "marks": [],
                          "value": " buttons",
                          "nodeType": "text"
                        }
                      ],
                      "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": " or ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {
                        "target": {
                          "sys": {
                            "id": "70YjtGRCs4BUACjaqQzlDY",
                            "type": "Link",
                            "linkType": "Entry"
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "data": {},
                          "marks": [],
                          "value": "links",
                          "nodeType": "text"
                        }
                      ],
                      "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": " change color on hover.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "Active and Focus States: Style elements differently when they are active (like a ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {
                        "target": {
                          "sys": {
                            "id": "FLAhUrwyFee8ZwKeQU40J",
                            "type": "Link",
                            "linkType": "Entry"
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "data": {},
                          "marks": [],
                          "value": "button",
                          "nodeType": "text"
                        }
                      ],
                      "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": " being clicked) or focused (like a form field when a user clicks into it).",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "Visited and Unvisited ",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {
                        "target": {
                          "sys": {
                            "id": "70YjtGRCs4BUACjaqQzlDY",
                            "type": "Link",
                            "linkType": "Entry"
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "data": {},
                          "marks": [],
                          "value": "Links",
                          "nodeType": "text"
                        }
                      ],
                      "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
                    },
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": ": Differentiate between links that a user has clicked (visited) and those they haven’t (unvisited), making it easier for users to navigate your content.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "First Child and Last Child: Style the first or last element in a list or group differently. This can be useful for adding unique touches to the first or last item in a menu or gallery.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "Nth-Child: Apply styles to specific elements based on their order in a list, such as every second or third item.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "data": {},
                      "marks": [],
                      "value": "Checked State: Style checkboxes or radio buttons differently when they are selected.",
                      "nodeType": "text"
                    }
                  ],
                  "nodeType": "paragraph"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "list-item"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "ordered-list"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "These pseudo-classes allow designers to create more dynamic, user-friendly, and visually appealing websites without needing to use JavaScript for basic interactive behaviors.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "nodeType": "document"
    },
    "codeField": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "css\n/* change button color to blue with white text on hover */\nbutton:hover {\n  background-color: blue;\n  color: white;\n}\n\n/* change button color to darkblue when the button is active (clicked) */\nbutton:active {\n  background-color: darkblue;\n}\n\n/* change input color to green when the input is in focus (clicked) */\ninput:focus {\n  border-color: green;\n}\n\n/* change link text color to blue when the link was already visited */\na:visited {\n  color: blue;\n}\n\n/* make first list item element bold */\nul li:first-child {\n  font-weight: bold;\n}\n\n/* make last list item element bold */\nul li:last-child {\n  font-weight: bold;\n}\n\n/* give every second item a lightgrey background */\nul li:nth-child(2n) { \n  background-color: lightgray;\n}\n\n/* give the third item a lightgrey background */\nul li:nth-child(3) {\n  font-style: italic;\n}\n\n/* give a checkbox a green outline when it's checked */\ninput[type=\"checkbox\"]:checked {\n  outline: 2px solid green;\n}",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
